  "description": "A write is a dead store where every path from it reaches another write before any read: both branches of an if statement, the code after a loop, and the next clause a switch clause falls into overwrite it, while a branch with no write keeps it. A statement after a try statement whose block leaves through its finally block is unreachable, and one after a catch block that falls through is not.",
